"notes": "Cash-basis village. Governmental figures from p4 Total column; beginning/ending cash are fund balances (beginning 'as previously reported'). Business-type from p6 enterprise funds cash receipts/disbursements statement; measure = cash (168,139 to 218,523); operating plus nonoperating expenses (Debt Service 94,226, Capital Outlay 1,366) counted as disbursements; printed business-type disbursements total 315,394 is from p2 (operating 219,802 + nonoperating 95,592), because p6 prints no combined total. Printed business receipts 365,778 = total operating revenues. Balance sheet is the cash-basis net position statement total column (p1); no liabilities. Only detail schedule is the all-funds budgetary comparison (p7), which mixes governmental and enterprise funds and whose printed totals (861,774 revenue, 706,736 expenditure) cover both fund types; items sum to those totals. Recategorization (attempt 4): earlier splits of p7 State 380,727, Local 372,876 and Capital Outlay 20,181 into pieces by matching p4/p6 amounts were removed because p7 does not print those breakdowns; each is now a single line with its printed budget (State 132,585; Local 527,350; Capital Outlay 89,700). Local fund_type set to business-type and Capital Outlay to governmental as the larger share, but both mix fund types (see review). Taxes ties to p4 property tax. Function/department lines have no object breakdown so detail_category is not itemized. Debt Service (p6/p7) combines principal and interest and is all categorized as principal."
